.DS_Store

# Inherited claude-template maintainer content — not part of this project.
# Disposition (delete/keep/move) is an open prerequisite decision (see spec Open Questions #7).
#
# NOTE (2026-07-28): /CLAUDE.md was previously listed in this block and has been REMOVED from it.
# It is not inherited content — the root CLAUDE.md is this project's primary operating document
# (36 hits for drone_video_ai / reference_pack / drone-video-examples, against 0 in the genuinely
# inherited README.md and TODO.md). Leaving it here would have excluded the one file that explains
# the project from the repository's first commit.
/README.md
/CHANGELOG.md
/TODO.md
/REVIEW.md
/PROMPTLAB-READINESS.md
/docs/
/promptlab/
/copilot-studio/
/assets/
/dist/
/site/
/mkdocs.yml
/sync-claude-template.sh
/requirements-promptlab.txt

# Raw footage over 100MB
/_01_examples/instagram_reel_v34_all_kb_full.mp4
/_01_examples/viral_test_v2_4k.mp4

# Pipeline outputs — regenerable from manifests + raw footage, per plan.md's
# retention convention (spec Open Question #2). data/manifests/ (small JSON)
# is intentionally NOT ignored — safe to commit selectively.
/data/interim/
/data/output/
/data/reference_pack/media/*
!/data/reference_pack/media/.gitkeep

# Working footage tree — 112 GB, 453 camera-original DJI .MP4/.SRT files from a July 2026 shoot
# (Khorog / Murghab / Langar / Karakul). This is primary capture, not a mirror and not regenerable.
# It must never enter git: it would exceed every practical repository limit and is the user's
# footage, not this project's measurement output. Added 2026-07-28 — it was previously unignored,
# so the repository's first `git add .` would have attempted to stage all 112 GB.
/00-WORKING/

# Hook activity log — appended to on every tool call, regenerable, and pure session noise.
# Root CLAUDE.md ("## Hooks") already describes this file as gitignored; until 2026-07-28 it was
# not, and that claim was stale. This rule makes the documentation true.
/.claude/activity.md

# Vendored Claude Code chat transcripts. Claude Code stores these under
# ~/.claude/projects/<slug>/, where <slug> is derived from the project's ABSOLUTE path, so
# relocating this repo (e.g. onto an SSD) silently orphans every prior session — /resume finds
# nothing and reports no error. Copied in on 2026-08-01 so the history travels with the folder.
# Gitignored deliberately: the remote is PUBLIC and raw transcripts contain absolute local
# paths and unreviewed session content. Durable across a move, never published.
/.claude/transcripts/

# Consolidated local copy of source drone footage (~3.8GB) — a convenience mirror of the
# read-only 00-assets/drone-video-examples/ and _archive/ trees (CLAUDE.md "Source footage"
# table). Never authoritative provenance and never committed; regenerate by re-copying.
/data/raw/

# Third-party best-in-class REFERENCE videos (targets to aim at, not source material).
# Never committed — these are all-rights-reserved works by other creators, held locally for
# study only. data/reference/REGISTRY.md (the curated catalogue) and data/reference/probe/
# (measurements about them) ARE tracked; the video files themselves never are.
/data/reference/videos/*
!/data/reference/videos/.gitkeep

# Python
/.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
/build/
.pytest_cache/

# Browser-automation scratch artifacts (e.g. reference-pack editorial_style
# "live_playback_review" attempts) — never intentional deliverables, and a
# frame-capture PNG of an all-rights-reserved source video is exactly the
# kind of footage-adjacent artifact this project's reference pack must never
# persist (spec Scope-out). Clean up loose ones at the repo root too.
/.playwright-mcp/
/seek*.png
/short*.png
/shot-initial.png
